From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wiaservc: the WIA service scans from SANE's scanners, for WIA 1 and WIA 2 (8301)

wiaservc: the WIA service scans from SANE's scanners, for WIA 1 and WIA 2

Windows' WIA device managers live in the WIA service (stisvc, wiaservc.dll in
svchost): programs create CLSID_WiaDevMgr and CLSID_WiaDevMgr2 out of process
(NAPS2's WIA driver asks for CLSCTX_LOCAL_SERVER and got "class not
registered" for WIA 2; WIA 1 listed no device). Both classes are now served by
the service only (AppID LocalService stisvc; the in-process registration that
Windows does not have is removed), and the service:
- lists SANE's devices (libsane, loaded when the service first looks); a device
  keeps its WIA device ID, {6BDD1FC6-810F-11D0-BEC7-08002BE2092F}\NNNN, the number
  of its key in the imaging device class, as Windows numbers a class's devices;
  its information properties (ID, name, manufacturer, type, port, version);
- builds a device's items: WIA 1 the root and its image item (the source chosen
  with the root's WIA_DPS_DOCUMENT_HANDLING_SELECT), WIA 2 the root and its
  Flatbed and Feeder items (WIA_CATEGORY_FLATBED/FEEDER), from the device's
  sources, modes, resolutions and bed;
- keeps their properties as a WIA driver does: ranges, lists and flags of valid
  values (GetPropertyAttributes), writes checked against them, values that follow
  (a new resolution keeps the area, the data type sets the depth, the intent sets
  type and resolution, sizes per line and per item), read by ID or name,
  enumerated, saved and restored as a property stream;
- scans: WIA 1 idtGetBandedData (a DIB: data header, data, end; progress while
  the device reads) and idtGetData (into the program's file), a feeder giving a
  page per transfer until WIA_ERROR_PAPER_EMPTY; WIA 2 IWiaTransfer::Download, a
  stream of the program's per page (WIA_IPS_PAGES, 0 for all), end of stream and
  of transfer; BMP, PNG, JPEG, TIFF and GIF; the picture of exactly the extents
  asked for; Cancel; device errors as WIA errors (paper empty or jammed, cover
  open, busy).
---
--- a/dlls/wiaservc/Makefile.in
+++ b/dlls/wiaservc/Makefile.in
@@ -1,11 +1,15 @@
 MODULE    = wiaservc.dll
-IMPORTS   = uuid ole32 advapi32
+UNIXLIB   = wiaservc.so
+IMPORTS   = uuid ole32 oleaut32 propsys advapi32
+UNIX_CFLAGS  = $(SANE_CFLAGS)
 
 EXTRADLLFLAGS = -Wb,--prefer-native
 
 SOURCES = \
+	device.c \
 	factory.c \
+	props.c \
 	rsrc.rc \
 	service.c \
-	wiadevmgr.c \
-	wiaservc.idl
+	unixlib.c \
+	wiadevmgr.c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/dlls/wiaservc/device.c
@@ -0,0 +1,2618 @@
